# What NOT to upload when deploying from the Vercel CLI.
#
# The CLI does not read .gitignore, so without this file it tries to upload the
# entire working tree — 13 GB here, most of it agent worktrees — and the upload
# aborts with a bare "Upload aborted" that says nothing about size.
#
# Vercel installs dependencies and builds on its own machines, so none of this
# needs to travel. Git-linked deploys ignore this file entirely; it only matters
# for `vercel deploy` from a laptop.

node_modules
.next
out
dist

# Agent worktrees: 9 GB of full repo copies, each with its own node_modules.
.claude/worktrees

.git
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Never upload local environment files. Vercel holds its own copies, and a
# .env.local landing in a build would override them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

.DS_Store
